The repository contains small, transformed aggregate calibration snapshots from
the following sources. Apache-2.0 covers Agent Economy code, not third-party
source content or service terms.

Federal Funds Effective Rate [FEDFUNDS]
- Source: Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System (US), H.15 Selected
  Interest Rates, retrieved through FRED, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis.
- Series and citation: https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/FEDFUNDS
- FRED Services Terms of Use: https://fred.stlouisfed.org/legal/terms/
- FRED labels this series "Public Domain: Citation Requested."
- The pinned snapshot uses the 2021-01-08 vintage and records January, April,
  and December 2020 monthly values. Preserve the source and FRED attribution;
  downstream use remains subject to current FRED and source-series terms.
- An explicit refresh reads FRED's current graph CSV, which may contain revised
  observations, and resets the manifest/payload vintage to the UTC retrieval
  date. It does not label current data as the original 2021 or an ALFRED vintage.

Civilian unemployment rate [LNS14000000]
- Source: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, Labor Force Statistics from the
  Current Population Survey.
- Series: https://data.bls.gov/timeseries/LNS14000000
- BLS copyright guidance: https://www.bls.gov/opub/copyright-information.htm
- BLS-published material is public domain except identified previously
  copyrighted photographs and illustrations; BLS requests source citation.
  The pinned snapshot uses the 2021-01-08 vintage and records January, April,
  and December 2020 monthly values.
